  "demo": [
    {
      "id": "intro",
      "t": 0.0,
      "title": "One plan for a whole steel group",
      "view": "overview",
      "text": "Aquila: 13 sites on four continents, 15 blast furnaces, 10 arc furnaces, 73 Mt of crude steel capacity a year. The same group also runs under conventional S&OP and site control rooms in parallel - same state, same events, same physics."
    },
    {
      "id": "map",
      "t": 1.0,
      "title": "The whole value chain in one twin",
      "view": "map",
      "text": "Ore and coke yards, scrap bays, furnaces, casters, mills, the lanes to twelve regional markets and the transfers between sites - every asset of the group, compiled from PLX code and the asset register."
    },
    {
      "id": "bf",
      "t": 5.2,
      "title": "Blast furnace off wind",
      "view": "overview",
      "text": "Duisburg loses its largest furnace for about 30 hours; both planning departments know when it is due back. PLYXIS re-plans the whole group at once - iron, slabs (Velsen and Dunkirk can ship slabs to Duisburg's strip mill) and markets. The Schedule shows what moved and why."
    },
    {
      "id": "explain",
      "t": 8.0,
      "title": "Why this site and not that one?",
      "view": "schedule",
      "text": "Every decision carries its reasons: delivered margin per market, the shadow price of iron, of rolling capacity and of each lane - computed from the model's gradients."
    },
    {
      "id": "storm",
      "t": 18.2,
      "title": "A port closes",
      "view": "map",
      "text": "No vessels at IJmuiden for 36 hours. The ore yard holds weeks of burden: nothing to do but watch it - the twin knows that and does not over-react."
    },
    {
      "id": "ercot",
      "t": 20.2,
      "title": "A price signal a day ahead",
      "view": "overview",
      "text": "ERCOT forecasts 1,500 USD/MWh tomorrow afternoon, and both worlds know it a day ahead. The conventional control room will stop the Texas arc furnace for the window (demand response); PLYXIS plans the furnace's heats and the billet yard around it."
    },
    {
      "id": "gas",
      "t": 26.2,
      "title": "Gas curtailed in India",
      "view": "schedule",
      "text": "Hazira's direct reduction loses half its gas. Its arc furnaces need more scrap - within the copper limit of their coil grades, measured by the lab - and merchant HBI where it pays."
    },
    {
      "id": "drift",
      "t": 30.0,
      "title": "Reality drifts - the twin follows",
      "view": "data",
      "text": "Furnaces use more coke and more power than the engineering data say, scrap carries more copper than the specs. The estimator re-calibrates every hour from the plant's own measurements."
    },
    {
      "id": "demand",
      "t": 50.2,
      "title": "Customers pull orders forward",
      "view": "overview",
      "text": "North American car makers want a quarter more coated coil for 40 hours. Which site supplies it, and what does it displace? PLYXIS answers that for the whole group in the next plan."
    },
    {
      "id": "scrap",
      "t": 60.2,
      "title": "Scrap jumps 19 %",
      "view": "overview",
      "text": "European scrap costs 470 USD/t. Each site's metallic mix - hot metal, scrap, HBI - is re-planned against the new price, within its heat and copper balances."
    },
    {
      "id": "value",
      "t": 95.5,
      "title": "Value",
      "view": "overview",
      "text": "Same group, same events. PLYXIS plans to the group's objective, profit after its internal carbon price, and runs Europe on more scrap and less hot metal: less CO2e and a better result after the carbon price, at an operating profit within a few per cent of a competent S&OP's."
    }
  ]
}